     * `company`). Each job (`jobs`) has `id`, `title`, `company`, `provider`, `url`, `applyUrl`,
     * `location` and `locations`, `country`, `remote`, `workplaceType` (remote / hybrid / onsite),
     * `department`, `team`, `employmentType`, `postedAt`, `updatedAt`, `requisitionId`, `salary`
     * and `salaryRanges` (min, max, currency, interval) where the ATS publishes pay,
     * `customFields` (the ATS's extra fields) and, with `include_description=true`,
     * `descriptionText` and `descriptionHtml`. A field the ATS does not expose is null. Filter
     * with `keyword` (title words), `location`, `department` and `remote`; `limit` caps the jobs
     * returned. The answer also carries the detected `provider`, `company`, `companyName`,
     * `boardUrl`, `totalJobs` on the board and `matchedJobs`. A link to one posting returns just
     * that posting with its description. Billed one unit per upstream request that returned data
     * (`pagesFetched`): one for a whole Greenhouse, Ashby, Workable or Recruitee board, one per
     * Lever (100 jobs), Workday (20 jobs) or SmartRecruiters (100 jobs) listing page, plus one per
     * Workday / SmartRecruiters posting whose description is read.
     *
     * @param string|null $url The company's career page on its ATS, e.g. 'https://job-
     * boards.greenhouse.io/stripe', 'https://jobs.lever.co/palantir',
     * 'https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ramp',
     * 'https://nvidia.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite',
     * 'https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/Ubisoft2', 'https://apply.workable.com/huggingface',
     * 'https://bunq.recruitee.com'. A link to one posting returns just that posting.
     * @param array{provider?: string, company?: string, keyword?: string, location?: string, department?: string, remote?: bool, limit?: int, include_description?: bool, proxy_country?: string} $options
     *   - provider: Instead of `url`: the ATS (greenhouse, lever, ashby, workday, smartrecruiters,
     * workable, recruitee), with `company`.
     *   - company: Instead of `url`: the company's board name on that ATS, as in its career URL:
     * Greenhouse token ('stripe'), Lever / Ashby / Workable / Recruitee slug, SmartRecruiters
     * company id ('Ubisoft2'), Workday '<tenant>.wd<N>/<site>'
     * ('nvidia.wd5/NVIDIAExternalCareerSite').
     *   - keyword: Only jobs whose title contains every word, e.g. 'software engineer'.
     *   - location: Only jobs in this place (city, region or country as the company writes it,
     * e.g. 'London', 'Germany', 'Remote'); case-insensitive.
     *   - department: Only jobs in this department or team, e.g. 'Engineering'.
     *   - remote: Only remote jobs. API default: false.
     *   - limit: How many jobs to return (1-2000). API default: 100.
     *   - include_description: Add each job's full description (`descriptionText`,
     * `descriptionHtml`). On Workday and SmartRecruiters this reads every posting separately (one
     * billed request each, at most 300 per call). API default: false.
     *   - proxy_country: Proxy country the requests are sent from (ISO-2, e.g. 'US', 'DE'). Leave
     * blank to let the API pick.
